.Dd September 23, 2026
.Dt ICOWM-A11Y 5
.Os icowm-1.0.1
.Sh NAME
.Nm a11y.json
.Nd timing and visual-feedback overrides for IcoWM
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa a11y.json
adjusts timings and visual feedback for people who find the defaults
hard to work with: a double click that has to be too quick, a focused
window whose border is too thin to pick out, an urgent window that
announces itself too fast or too faintly.
.Pp
The file is optional, and every key within it is too.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic is-enabled Pq boolean, default Ql false
Whether anything in this file is honored at all.
While false the rest is read but not applied, so a set of overrides can
be kept ready and switched on when wanted.
.It Ic interaction.double-click-ms Pq integer, default Ql 400
How long, in milliseconds, may pass between two clicks for them to count
as a double click.
Raise it when two deliberate clicks keep being read as one.
.It Ic focus-indicator.min-border-width Pq integer, default Ql 0
A floor, in pixels, under the border width of the focused window,
whatever the theme asks for.
Zero leaves the theme alone.
.It Ic urgency.sound-bell Pq boolean, default Ql false
Whether the X bell rings when a window demands attention.
.Pp
IcoWM only asks for it.
Whether anything is heard rests with the X server, which is silent
until
.Xr xset 1
gives the bell a non-zero volume, and on many systems with a sound
daemon standing between the server and the speakers.
Turning this on and hearing nothing usually means the bell itself is
off, not that the setting was ignored.
.It Ic urgency.blink-interval-ms Pq integer, default Ql 600
How long, in milliseconds, each half of the urgency blink lasts.
A longer interval blinks more slowly, which is easier to follow and
less likely to trouble someone sensitive to flashing.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/icowm/a11y.json
The file this page describes, at the first of the several locations
.Xr icowm 1
looks in.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A slower double click, a border thick enough to see, and a slow blink
with the bell:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "is-enabled": true,
    "interaction": { "double-click-ms": 750 },
    "focus-indicator": { "min-border-width": 4 },
    "urgency": {
        "sound-bell": true,
        "blink-interval-ms": 1200
    }
}
.Ed
